WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.651 --> 00:00:01.619
- Good morning, believe nation,

00:00:01.619 --> 00:00:04.402
my name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is Believe,

00:00:04.402 --> 00:00:06.619
and I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:06.619 --> 00:00:09.359
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:09.359 --> 00:00:10.448
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.448 --> 00:00:13.351
today's message is don't
focus on the money.

00:00:13.351 --> 00:00:15.691
Over to you, Bob Marley.

00:00:15.691 --> 00:00:17.654
(rooster crows)

00:00:17.654 --> 00:00:19.951
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.951 --> 00:00:23.055
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:25.796
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:25.796 --> 00:00:27.810
- [Interviewer] Do you make a lot of money

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.839
out of your music?

00:00:29.839 --> 00:00:30.672
- Money?

00:00:32.096 --> 00:00:35.481
I mean, what is a lot of money to you?

00:00:35.481 --> 00:00:36.852
- [Interviewer] That's a good question.

00:00:36.852 --> 00:00:40.398
Have you made, say, millions of dollars?

00:00:40.398 --> 00:00:41.688
- No.

00:00:41.688 --> 00:00:43.864
- [Interviewer] Are you a rich man?

00:00:43.864 --> 00:00:44.831
- What do you mean, rich?

00:00:44.831 --> 00:00:46.202
What do you mean?

00:00:46.202 --> 00:00:47.612
- [Interviewer] Do you
have a lot of possessions?

00:00:47.612 --> 00:00:48.580
A lot of money in the bank?

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.393
- Possessions make you rich?

00:00:50.393 --> 00:00:51.965
I don't have that type of richness.

00:00:51.965 --> 00:00:54.382
My richness is life, forever.

00:00:55.432 --> 00:00:56.924
- If you just focus on the money,

00:00:56.924 --> 00:00:58.173
you're never going to get it.

00:00:58.173 --> 00:00:59.543
That's what so many entrepreneurs do,

00:00:59.543 --> 00:01:00.994
and why so many entrepreneurs fail,

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.888
is their number one goal is money.

00:01:02.888 --> 00:01:04.380
Now money is important.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.516
If you're running a
business, money is important.

00:01:06.516 --> 00:01:07.926
You know, even if you're
running a charity,

00:01:07.926 --> 00:01:08.853
money is still important.

00:01:08.853 --> 00:01:09.941
Money is important.

00:01:09.941 --> 00:01:11.353
It's just not the number one thing.

00:01:11.353 --> 00:01:12.885
It's the number two or three.

00:01:12.885 --> 00:01:14.819
There has to be something
more important than money

00:01:14.819 --> 00:01:17.237
for you to have success, ultimate success,

00:01:17.237 --> 00:01:18.890
as an entrepreneur.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.018
Sure you can make a few bucks,

00:01:20.018 --> 00:01:21.469
but you look at the people who
are at the top in any field,

00:01:21.469 --> 00:01:24.469
money was never the number one goal.

00:01:25.379 --> 00:01:27.313
Now in this clip, Bob
Marley is talking about

00:01:27.313 --> 00:01:28.965
how he's not rich financially,

00:01:28.965 --> 00:01:30.537
but he's rich in life.

00:01:30.537 --> 00:01:32.956
I'm saying you can be rich financially,

00:01:32.956 --> 00:01:34.689
and you can be rich in life,

00:01:34.689 --> 00:01:36.382
by not focusing on the money.

00:01:36.382 --> 00:01:38.962
Look at the people who
are self-made millionaires

00:01:38.962 --> 00:01:41.541
and billionaires, and
read their biographies,

00:01:41.541 --> 00:01:43.113
and read their story, to understand

00:01:43.113 --> 00:01:44.403
why they started their companies.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:45.733
Watch the top 10 videos on all of them.

00:01:45.733 --> 00:01:48.554
It's never been about the money.

00:01:48.554 --> 00:01:51.617
It's always been about
making a profound change

00:01:51.617 --> 00:01:54.156
in the way something is
done in their industry.

00:01:54.156 --> 00:01:55.687
Having a deep passion for their craft,

00:01:55.687 --> 00:01:58.710
that they needed to bring
this thing out into creation.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.412
You know, when George
Lucas created Star Wars,

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:03.669
he thought it would be a flop.

00:02:03.669 --> 00:02:05.885
He thought it would be
for a select few geeks

00:02:05.885 --> 00:02:08.345
who really loved that genre.

00:02:08.345 --> 00:02:09.905
He never expected it to be this huge thing

00:02:09.905 --> 00:02:11.961
that turned him into a billionaire.

00:02:11.961 --> 00:02:13.694
But he loved making the video.

00:02:13.694 --> 00:02:15.265
He poured every ounce of creativity he had

00:02:15.265 --> 00:02:17.182
into making that movie.

00:02:18.087 --> 00:02:19.699
And that's a story over and over

00:02:19.699 --> 00:02:21.393
and over and over and over again.

00:02:21.393 --> 00:02:24.820
Successful entrepreneurs love their craft.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.391
They want to do the work.

00:02:26.391 --> 00:02:29.213
And as a result of creating
something valuable,

00:02:29.213 --> 00:02:30.786
because they put so much love into it,

00:02:30.786 --> 00:02:32.559
then they start making money.

00:02:32.559 --> 00:02:34.977
And so, I don't want you
to be the entrepreneur

00:02:34.977 --> 00:02:37.114
who says I don't care about money,

00:02:37.114 --> 00:02:39.411
money is never important to me,

00:02:39.411 --> 00:02:41.587
because then you don't
go out and get money,

00:02:41.587 --> 00:02:43.483
and then you can't have the impact.

00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:45.740
Like, you need money to go
out and hire more people,

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.070
and have an even bigger impact.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.238
There's only so much you can do.

00:02:48.238 --> 00:02:50.092
It's great to spend
half your time working,

00:02:50.092 --> 00:02:52.470
half your time volunteering,
and giving back,

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:55.049
that's awesome, but you
could have a bigger impact

00:02:55.049 --> 00:02:58.233
and volunteer more if you
had a team of 100 people,

00:02:58.233 --> 00:03:01.579
who are also spreading out
their time volunteering.

00:03:01.579 --> 00:03:02.667
So money is important.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:05.046
The people that think money is the devil,

00:03:05.046 --> 00:03:06.094
and you shouldn't have money,

00:03:06.094 --> 00:03:07.504
you're never going to
be successful either.

00:03:07.504 --> 00:03:08.834
Money is important.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.569
It's just not the number one thing.

00:03:10.569 --> 00:03:12.745
Don't start a business
just trying to make money.

00:03:12.745 --> 00:03:14.639
Start a business to have a profound impact

00:03:14.639 --> 00:03:16.372
on the way things are
done in the industry,

00:03:16.372 --> 00:03:18.105
and to help people.

00:03:18.105 --> 00:03:19.596
That thing has to be above.

00:03:19.596 --> 00:03:20.926
For me, it's helping entrepreneurs.

00:03:20.926 --> 00:03:22.337
I believe that entrepreneurs will solve

00:03:22.337 --> 00:03:24.231
all of the major problems in the world.

00:03:24.231 --> 00:03:25.562
It's not on the government,

00:03:25.562 --> 00:03:27.094
it's not on corporations,

00:03:27.094 --> 00:03:30.036
it's us, we're going
to make the difference.

00:03:30.036 --> 00:03:31.447
And so for me, making these videos

00:03:31.447 --> 00:03:33.019
and helping by writing books,

00:03:33.019 --> 00:03:35.235
and doing the things that I do,

00:03:35.235 --> 00:03:37.212
I feel helps entrepreneurs,

00:03:37.212 --> 00:03:40.356
and helps contribute to solving

00:03:40.356 --> 00:03:42.331
all the major problems of the world.

00:03:42.331 --> 00:03:44.025
You guys out there are
going to be the ones

00:03:44.025 --> 00:03:45.398
who are making a difference.

00:03:45.398 --> 00:03:46.446
If I can motivate you,

00:03:46.446 --> 00:03:47.776
or if I can give you
strategies to help you,

00:03:47.776 --> 00:03:50.154
if you keep on that extra year,

00:03:50.154 --> 00:03:51.564
and that's the year
that makes a difference,

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:54.184
that makes me feel good,

00:03:54.184 --> 00:03:55.433
it makes me feel like
I'm having an impact.

00:03:55.433 --> 00:03:57.369
That's why I do what I do.

00:03:57.369 --> 00:03:58.820
And in the process, I make money.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:02.085
If I wasn't making money,
I couldn't hire a team,

00:04:02.085 --> 00:04:03.334
and I'd be doing everything myself,

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.389
and I'd be down to one
video every two weeks,

00:04:05.389 --> 00:04:07.485
which isn't good for anybody.

00:04:07.485 --> 00:04:09.622
So money is never the number one goal,

00:04:09.622 --> 00:04:12.282
but it's also not the number 100 goal.

00:04:12.282 --> 00:04:15.305
It's got to be two or three on the list.

00:04:15.305 --> 00:04:16.595
So the question today is, I'm curious,

00:04:16.595 --> 00:04:19.295
what is the number one thing on your list

00:04:19.295 --> 00:04:20.128
that you would put ahead of making money?

00:04:20.128 --> 00:04:23.156
Leave in the comments below,

00:04:23.156 --> 00:04:24.769
really curious to find out.

00:04:24.769 --> 00:04:26.381
Also want to give a quick
shout-out to Mike Markham

00:04:26.381 --> 00:04:28.355
from restaurant-hr.com, Mike,

00:04:28.355 --> 00:04:30.532
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:04:30.532 --> 00:04:33.395
Your One Word, and making a review on it.

00:04:33.395 --> 00:04:34.765
I'm really glad you enjoyed it,

00:04:34.765 --> 00:04:37.425
and I really want to thank
you for your support.

00:04:37.425 --> 00:04:38.716
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:04:38.716 --> 00:04:39.844
I believe in you,

00:04:39.844 --> 00:04:41.698
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:43.795
and whatever your one word is,

00:04:43.795 --> 00:04:45.770
much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning,

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:49.075
for another shot of inspresso.

00:04:49.075 --> 00:04:51.656
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:51.656 --> 00:04:55.415
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:04:55.415 --> 00:04:58.873
(typewriter clicking)

00:04:58.873 --> 00:05:00.588
- I never did anything for money, right.

00:05:00.588 --> 00:05:03.410
So I was there but it
was never about money.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:07.077
My experience has been when
people do things for money,

00:05:07.077 --> 00:05:08.810
you make bad choices.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:10.585
You find what you love,
and then you'll learn

00:05:10.585 --> 00:05:13.930
how to make money doing what you love.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.066
When I changed careers,

00:05:16.066 --> 00:05:19.492
I was never changing
to something for money,

00:05:19.492 --> 00:05:22.514
I was changing to something
I loved more, right.

00:05:22.514 --> 00:05:24.288
And that to me, that's really the only way

00:05:24.288 --> 00:05:26.585
to keep the passion.

00:05:26.585 --> 00:05:29.446
If you have two choices, and
one is playing the piano,

00:05:29.446 --> 00:05:31.696
and another one is bowling,

00:05:33.719 --> 00:05:36.661
and you can make more money bowling,

00:05:36.661 --> 00:05:38.394
but you love playing the piano more,

00:05:38.394 --> 00:05:40.249
you got to play the piano.

00:05:40.249 --> 00:05:41.700
It's like you'll tear yourself apart

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.085
if you're not doing the thing
that you love most in life.

00:05:45.085 --> 00:05:46.496
And you know what it is right now.

00:05:46.496 --> 00:05:48.632
Right now there's something that you love

00:05:48.632 --> 00:05:50.969
more than everything.

00:05:50.969 --> 00:05:52.743
Whatever it is that you love, crazy,

00:05:52.743 --> 00:05:55.241
has to be the thing that
you dedicate your life to.

00:05:55.241 --> 00:05:57.418
- You make more money than
any actor in the world.

00:05:57.418 --> 00:05:59.313
- This, too, shall pass.

00:05:59.313 --> 00:06:01.691
By the way, I don't even
know if that's true.

00:06:01.691 --> 00:06:05.682
I can tell you I pay more taxes
than anybody I've ever met.

00:06:05.682 --> 00:06:10.277
Truth be told, I've never,
ever been motivated by money.

00:06:10.277 --> 00:06:11.809
- I got to give it to you, man,

00:06:11.809 --> 00:06:14.589
because you just seem
like such a normal guy.

00:06:14.589 --> 00:06:16.403
How are you able,
- That is my superpower.

00:06:16.403 --> 00:06:17.598
Talk to my wife.
- Exactly.

00:06:17.598 --> 00:06:18.689
That's what it is.

00:06:18.689 --> 00:06:20.018
Make people believe
you're a normal person.

00:06:20.018 --> 00:06:21.884
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:21.884 --> 00:06:22.717
- When you start out, you have to deal

00:06:22.717 --> 00:06:25.811
with the problems of failure.

00:06:25.811 --> 00:06:27.987
You need to be thick-skinned,

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.763
to learn that not every
project will survive.

00:06:30.763 --> 00:06:32.639
A freelance life, a life in the arts,

00:06:32.639 --> 00:06:34.533
is sometimes like putting
messages in bottles

00:06:34.533 --> 00:06:37.637
on a desert island and
hoping that someone will find

00:06:37.637 --> 00:06:40.175
one of your bottles, and open it,

00:06:40.175 --> 00:06:42.634
and read it, and put something in a bottle

00:06:42.634 --> 00:06:45.576
that will wash its way back to you.

00:06:45.576 --> 00:06:49.566
Appreciation or a commission
or money, or love,

00:06:49.566 --> 00:06:51.501
and you have to accept
that you may put out

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:52.951
hundreds of things for every bottle

00:06:52.951 --> 00:06:55.118
that winds up coming back.

00:06:56.861 --> 00:07:00.248
The problems of failure, the
problems of discouragement,

00:07:00.248 --> 00:07:02.263
of hopelessness, of hunger,

00:07:02.263 --> 00:07:03.955
you want everything to
happen and you want it now

00:07:03.955 --> 00:07:06.293
and things go wrong.

00:07:06.293 --> 00:07:08.227
My first book, a piece of journalism

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:10.686
I'd done only for the money,

00:07:10.686 --> 00:07:13.709
and which had already bought
me an electric typewriter,

00:07:13.709 --> 00:07:17.255
from the advance, should
have been a bestseller.

00:07:17.255 --> 00:07:18.666
It should have paid me a lot of money,

00:07:18.666 --> 00:07:21.084
if the publisher hadn't gone
into involuntary liquidation

00:07:21.084 --> 00:07:23.220
between the first print run selling out

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.640
and the second print run never happening

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:28.985
and before any royalties could be paid.

00:07:28.985 --> 00:07:30.637
It would have done.

00:07:30.637 --> 00:07:32.128
And I shrugged.

00:07:32.128 --> 00:07:34.184
And I still had my electric typewriter.

00:07:34.184 --> 00:07:36.239
And enough money to pay the
rent for a couple of months,

00:07:36.239 --> 00:07:38.417
and I decided that I'd
do my best in future

00:07:38.417 --> 00:07:41.584
not to write books just for the money.

00:07:42.649 --> 00:07:44.341
If you didn't get the money
then you didn't have anything,

00:07:44.341 --> 00:07:46.639
and if I did work I was proud of,

00:07:46.639 --> 00:07:48.009
and I didn't get the money,

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:50.749
well, at least I'd have the work.

00:07:50.749 --> 00:07:53.047
Every now and then, I forget that rule.

00:07:53.047 --> 00:07:55.586
And whenever I do, the
universe kicks me hard

00:07:55.586 --> 00:07:56.836
and reminds me.

00:07:59.213 --> 00:08:01.510
I don't know that it's an
issue for anybody but me,

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:03.486
but it's true that nothing I did

00:08:03.486 --> 00:08:06.267
where the only reason for
doing it was the money

00:08:06.267 --> 00:08:10.184
was ever worth it, except
as bitter experience.

00:08:11.833 --> 00:08:14.669
Usually I didn't wind up
getting the money, either.

00:08:14.669 --> 00:08:16.394
(congregation laughs)

00:08:16.394 --> 00:08:18.489
The things I did because I was excited,

00:08:18.489 --> 00:08:20.223
and wanted to see them exist in reality,

00:08:20.223 --> 00:08:21.593
have never let me down,
and I've never regretted

00:08:21.593 --> 00:08:24.260
the time I spend on any of them.

